Watching the progress of a rolling restart<pre><code>kubectl get storageclusterops roll-simplyblock-cluster -n simplyblock -o wide -w
</code></pre> Reading the position of the walk<pre><code>kubectl get storageclusterops roll-simplyblock-cluster -n simplyblock \
    -o jsonpath='{.status}' | jq '{phase, step, rollingRestart}'
</code></pre> Example of the rolling restart status<pre><code>{
  "phase": "Running",
  "rollingRestart": {
    "nodeIndex": 1,
    "nodes": [
      "114899a6-d708-499e-8051-bc9ca9713cf8",
      "82198a36-fcbb-43e3-949c-0260bf40f0ac",
      "707dd443-5d0e-470f-bdde-92f1238c4b01"
    ]
  },
  "step": {
    "deadline": "2026-09-25T14:52:10Z",
    "state": "Rebalancing"
  }
}
</code></pre> <p>A <code>NodeRestarted</code> event is emitted each time the walk advances to the next node.</p>
